      "message": "The subject says this provides an accessor, but `vma_file_offset()` has been in `include/linux/p3s/vma.h` since aosp/4312510 (`fs/proc` and the coredump code use it). So the patch only converts two callers, and as far as I can see neither conversion changes behavior (see the inline comments).\n\nWould it be OK to drop this patch? If the `vb2_mmap()` slice check makes sense, it could take its place with a subject that describes it.",
