        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T03:10:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this doesn\u0027t change anything: `__find_plane_by_offset()` decodes the buffer and plane from `offset \u003e\u003e PAGE_SHIFT`, and this file doesn\u0027t include `\u003clinux/p3s_user_pages.h\u003e`, so the slice offset that `vma_file_offset()` adds (below 16KB) is dropped again.\n\nIf the aim is to make `vb2_mmap()` P3S-aware, I think the useful part would be rejecting a slice: offsets are page-aligned cookies, and `vma-\u003evm_pgoff \u003d 0` below doesn\u0027t reset `vm_slice_off`, so the memops would still start the mapping at that slice. Could we return `-EINVAL` for a non-zero `vma_slice_off(vma)`, as `perf_mmap()` does since aosp/4368055 (and as suggested for GEM on aosp/4367607)?\n\nOtherwise, would it be OK to drop this hunk?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "fb0dfbe5551e6d51bfbf4b55414536e9b0b39759",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
